※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4670 LANG_ITERATOR_DOES_NOT_LEAVE
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4670 LANG_ITERATOR_DOES_NOT_LEAVE
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4203 LANG_TYPE_INITIALIZER_MISMATCH

※ A walk that does not say it is kept in `⎕heap` is described in the room of
※ the call that started it: it is neither a field nor answered, and it does not
※ stand where one kept in the heap is wanted.

fn upto(n: u8) ⇉ u8:
    yield n

type J = walk : ⌖⇉u8

fn out() → ⌖⇉u8:
    ⎕start(upto(1u8))

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let v: ⌖⇉u8 in ⎕heap = ⎕start(upto(2u8))
    0u6
